.SS "\fBt_ast\fP * parser_parse (t_list * tokens, \fBt_shell\fP * shell)"

.PP
consume a t_list* of tokens and return the AST root\&. Returns NULL on syntax error (error printed to stderr)\&.

.PP
The token list is NOT freed here, caller frees it with \fBlexer_free_tokens()\fP\&.

.PP
consume a t_list* of tokens and return the AST root\&.

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fItokens\fP pointer on a struct s_list of tokens 
.br
\fIshell\fP pointer on a struct s_shell
.RE
.PP
this is the main function of the parser module

.PP
call parse list which wrap all the layers and check for EOF

.PP
parse_list (";" and "&" separators) -> parse_and_or

.PP
parse_and_or ("&&" and "||" separators) -> parse_pipeline

.PP
parse_pipeline ("|" separator) -> parse_command

.PP
parse_command (read simple command) -> parse_subshell

.PP
parse_subshell recurse on parse_list

.PP
parse_heredoc walk ast and collect heredocs

.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
\fBt_ast\fP struct 
.RE
.PP

